From: Bellatrix Development <bellatrix@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] usb2otg: only schedule work for due SOF transfers

handle_SOF records whether it promoted an interrupt request, but used to
Cause PendingInt unconditionally.  That woke the scheduler at the 1 kHz SOF
rate even when the mouse, hub and every other periodic endpoint were waiting
for a later frame.

Only request pending work after an actual promotion.  Split-channel delay and
stall handling remain in the SOF handler itself and therefore keep their
existing frame-sensitive behaviour.

---
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c
@@ -966,7 +966,8 @@ static void handle_SOF(struct USB2OTGUnit *USBUnit, struct ExecBase *SysBase, ULONG frnm_orig)
 #endif
         }
 
-        FNAME_DEV(Cause)(USB2OTGBase, &USBUnit->hu_PendingInt);
+        if (int_scheduled)
+            FNAME_DEV(Cause)(USB2OTGBase, &USBUnit->hu_PendingInt);
 
         /*
          * Do NOT arm INT channels from here: arming a direct periodic
-- 
